          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "书房 (shūfáng) is built from 书 'book' and 房 (fáng) 'room', both inherited from Middle Chinese, syo and bjang (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'a room': the room for books."
